<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong Countdown Outlook.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong Countdown Outlook.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a calendar counting down to the handover of the British colony of Hong Kong to China at midnight on June 30.</p>
<p>======================================================</p>
<p>APRIL 21</p>
<p>- Advance guard of China's PLA troops arrives in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>======================================================</p>
<p>APRIL 27</p>
<p>- Opening of Lantau Link suspension bridge, providing road and rail link for new Chek Lap Lok airport due to open in 1998.</p>
<p>======================================================= JUNE 3/4</p>
<p>- Hong Kong democracy movement to commemorate 1989 Beijing massacre with overnight candlelight vigil in Victoria Park.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JUNE 9</p>
<p>- Dragon Boat Festival Holiday</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JUNE 28</p>
<p>- Official Birthday of Queen Elizabeth. Public Holiday.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JUNE 30</p>
<p>- Last day of British colonial rule. Public holiday.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JULY 1</p>
<p>- China resumes sovereignty of Hong Kong. Public holiday.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JULY 2</p>
<p>- Public holiday to mark China's resumption of sovereignty.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>DECEMBER 1999</p>
<p>- Administration of Portuguese-run Macau reverts to China.</p>
<p>========================================================</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6352</p>
